   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,574:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  attack simulations.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,576:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  14 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,578:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Test Suite
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,583:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Automated verification of allowed traffic, blocked ports, state tracking, and unsolicited
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,586:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: packet drops.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,588:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  15 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,590:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Packet Path Validation
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,594:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Traced transit across veth pairs, bridges, XDP, and routing FIB.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,596:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  16 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,598:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Expandable Platform
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,601:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Modular foundation for rate limiting, SYN cookies, and machine learning
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,603:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: telemetry.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,606:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 🚀 Quick Start
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,835:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Install Dependencies 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Verify Environment (Step 1)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: bash scripts/setup.sh
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. Initialize Container Lab 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 Networks (Steps 2 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,847:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: bash scripts/setup_env.sh
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,848:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. Build eBPF Dataplane 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,848:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,849:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Userspace Utility
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,850:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: make
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,851:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. Start the Stateful Firewall
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,853:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Attach to the untrusted bridge interface
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/fw-ctl -i incus-untrust -m hybrid -d both
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:08:59,857:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 🛠️ CLI Management with 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,077:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (Step 10)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,078:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,079:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  communicates directly with kernel eBPF maps:
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # View active rules
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule list
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Add a rule to allow HTTP web traffic
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule add --proto tcp --dport 80 --action
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,088:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: allow --desc "HTTP Web"
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Add a rule to allow iperf3 benchmarks
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,093:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule add --proto tcp --dport 5201 --action
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,094:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: allow --desc "iperf3"
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,095:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Add a rule to allow ICMP ping
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,098:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule add --proto icmp --action allow
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,099:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: --desc "Ping Echo"
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,100:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Load rules from YAML configuration
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,102:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule load config/rules.yaml
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,103:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Delete a rule by ID
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule del 1
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: # Flush all active rules
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,107:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sudo ./build/firewallctl rule flush
