   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,920:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Comprehensive Stateful eBPF/XDP Firewall Architecture 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,922:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Implementation Guide
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,926:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Overview 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,928:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Core Philosophy
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,931:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This project implements a high-performance, kernel-native stateful firewall using 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: eBPF (Extended Berkeley
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Packet Filter)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  and 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP (eXpress Data Path)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,959:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  on Linux. The system provides sub-microsecond packet
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: classification, line-rate throughput, stateful TCP/UDP/ICMP flow tracking, and dynamic rule management from
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,966:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: userspace without kernel recompilation.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The architecture strictly follows a 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: split dataplane/control-plane model
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,971:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Kernel Dataplane (eBPF/XDP)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,977:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Fast-path packet parsing, state validation, rule matching, and
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,978:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: line-rate enforcement (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,980:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP_PASS
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  / 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP_DROP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,983:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,984:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Userspace Control Plane (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,987:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,988:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  / 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,989:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fw-ctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,990:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: )
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,994:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Rule configuration, connection state
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,996:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: inspection, telemetry aggregation, and lifecycle management.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,998:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. The 16-Step Design 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:00,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,001:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Architecture Blueprint
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,003:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,019:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                                      LINUX HOST (Step 1 & Step 4)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,021:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                                   |
