   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |        (Attacks / Out-of-State)               |                  
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,530:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            |                     |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,546:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                                               v                  
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,548:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            |                     |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,564:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                               +-------------------------------+  
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,566:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:            |                     |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,580:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                               | Host IPv4 Routing Plane (FIB)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,581:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |--------------+                     |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,597:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                               |  (net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1)    |  
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,598:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                                  |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,613:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |                               +-------------------------------+  
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,614:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:                                  |
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,616:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 1: Set up one Linux machine as the host
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,620:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,622:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All components, virtual network bridges, containers, and kernel hooks run on a single host.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,623:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,624:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Host requirements: Linux Kernel >= 5.15 with BTF support (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,625:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,627:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ),
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,628:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Clang/LLVM toolchain, and 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,630:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ip_forward=1
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,632:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,634:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 2: Create virtual machines/containers using Incus
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,636:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,650:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Incus provisions lightweight system containers that provide isolated network namespaces and
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,653:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: individual IP addresses without the virtualization overhead of full virtual machines.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,654:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,656:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Containers: 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,657:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: client
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (10.10.1.20), 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: attacker
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (10.10.1.10), 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: webserver
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (10.10.2.10), 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,666:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: admin
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (10.10.99.10).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 3: Organise containers into three networks
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,674:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Untrusted Segment (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incus-untrust
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,678:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  - 10.10.1.0/24)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,680:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Houses clients and the attacker simulator.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,682:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Protected Segment (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,685:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incus-protect
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,687:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  - 10.10.2.0/24)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,689:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Houses target services (Nginx, backend
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,691:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: applications).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,693:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Management Segment (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,696:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incus-mgmt
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,698:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  - 10.10.99.0/24)
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Isolated network for administration and
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: monitoring to prevent operator lockout during aggressive firewall policy tests.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,709:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 4: Connect networks through the Linux host, not through a container
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,710:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Container networks are joined on the host via bridge interfaces and 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: veth
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,714:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  pairs.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,715:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,716:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The host routing engine (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ) routes traffic across subnets.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The firewall attaches directly to this forwarding path on the host, operating at the bare-metal kernel
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: driver layer.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 5: Attach the firewall using XDP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The XDP hook (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: xdp_firewall_prog
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,736:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ) intercepts incoming packets at the network device driver
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,738:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: layer (or generic SKB fallback) prior to 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sk_buff
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,745:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  allocation or netfilter traversal, saving up to 90%
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,746:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: of kernel CPU overhead during high packet loads.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,748:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 6: Write the firewall logic in eBPF
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,750:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The kernel fast-path executes a four-stage pipeline:
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,751:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,753:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Parser
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,754:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Validates Ethernet, IPv4, TCP/UDP/ICMP headers.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,756:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,757:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: State Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,759:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Validates connection state (TCP handshake, sequence tracking, UDP flow activity).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rule Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Evaluates user-defined policies for initial connection establishment.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Decision 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,770:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Telemetry Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Returns 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,772:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP_PASS
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  or 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,775:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP_DROP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,778:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  and emits telemetry events to
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the BPF ring buffer.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 7: Parse each packet into its five identifying fields
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,786:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For every packet, extracts: 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src_ip
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,789:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,790:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dst_ip
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,792:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,793:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: src_port
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,795:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,796:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dst_port
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,798:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: proto
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,801:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,802:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Validates TCP control flags (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,805:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SYN
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,807:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,808:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ACK
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: FIN
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,813:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,815:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: RST
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,816:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PSH
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,820:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: URG
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,823:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,825:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 8: Keep firewall rules outside the eBPF program
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,827:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,829:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rules are stored in a dedicated 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,831:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,834:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: rules_map
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,836:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Each entry defines subnet masks, port ranges, protocol filters, actions (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ALLOW
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: DROP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,847:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ), and hit
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,849:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: counters.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,850:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,852:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rules can be updated dynamically via 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,853:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  without rebuilding or reloading the eBPF
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,856:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: kernel program.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,858:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 9: Add connection state to make it a stateful firewall
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,859:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Flow states are tracked in 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: conntrack_map
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: BPF_MAP_TYPE_HASH
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,864:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: TCP State Machine
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,868:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,869:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,870:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SYN
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,871:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (new flow allowed by rule) -> 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CONN_STATE_SYN_SENT
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,875:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,876:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: SYN-ACK
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,877:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (from server) -> 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,879:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CONN_STATE_SYN_RECV
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,882:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ACK
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (handshake complete) -> 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,884:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CONN_STATE_ESTABLISHED
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,886:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (Fast-path allow).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: FIN
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,889:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  / 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,890:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: RST
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,891:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  -> 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,892:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CONN_STATE_FIN_WAIT
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,893:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  / 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,895:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CONN_STATE_CLOSED
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,896:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,898:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Unsolicited out-of-state packets
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (e.g. non-SYN packets with no prior state) are
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,902:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dropped immediately (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,903:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: XDP_DROP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,905:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ).
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,906:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,907:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: UDP 
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,908:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: &
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,909:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  ICMP
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,911:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Pseudo-connection state tracking with automatic inactivity timeouts.
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,913:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Step 10: Build the userspace control tool (
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,914:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: )
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,916:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,917:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: firewallctl
   DEBUG: 2026-09-04 00:09:01,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  interacts with BPF maps via 
